# Frontend environment — for running the frontend directly, outside
# docker-compose: `npm run dev`, or building/running this service's Docker
# image by itself (`docker build` / `docker run`, no compose).
#
# Running via `docker compose up` instead? BACKEND_URL is already wired
# into ../docker-compose.yml's `frontend:` service from the repo-root .env
# file — copy ../.env.example to ../.env and edit there, not here.
# (docker-compose does not read this file, and `npm run dev` doesn't use
# BACKEND_URL at all — see the note below.)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in this directory and adjust as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env

# Only used by `npm run dev` (the Vite dev server) or a production build
# (`npm run build` / the Docker image's build stage) — Vite bakes VITE_*
# vars into the JS bundle at build time, so this can't be changed after
# building without rebuilding.
#
# Leave unset for local `npm run dev`: the dev server already proxies /api
# to http://localhost:8000 on its own (see vite.config.ts), no env var
# needed. Only set this for a split-service deployment (e.g. Render/Railway,
# frontend and backend each with their own public URL) where you want the
# browser to call the backend's public URL directly instead of going through
# nginx's proxy below — set it as a build-time variable on that platform,
# not a regular service env var (see frontend/Dockerfile).
#VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.example.com/api/v1

# Only used by the Docker image at container *start* (nginx's built-in
# envsubst-on-templates step — see nginx.conf.template), never by
# `npm run dev` and never baked in at build time. Where nginx's /api/ proxy
# forwards to.
#
# "http://backend:8000" (the default, baked into frontend/Dockerfile) only
# resolves inside a docker-compose network where a service is literally
# named "backend" — running this image standalone (no compose), point this
# at wherever your backend is actually reachable instead.
BACKEND_URL=http://backend:8000
